{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435800-the-ki-en-gir-are-not-from-canaan","id":1435800,"title":"The Ki-En-Gir are not from Canaan","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-17T17:27:52-08:00","id":1435800,"title":"The Ki-En-Gir are not from Canaan","content":"Okay, this was pointed out WAAAAAAY back in the first manuscript and we were given vague assurances it would be correct by this go round. Well, it hasn't been. Its very sloppy and it should be corrected as swiftly as possible.<br /> <br /> &quot;Canaan\u2019s own legions of professional soldiers, the Ki-En-Gir, had heeded the warnings of Irem\u2019s relentless campaign<br /> well in advance.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a badly misunderstood reading of the first edition's history and a horribly researched bit of writing to boot. Ki-En-Gir, as noted many times by us and confirmed by the writers of first edition, refer to the 4000 Millenia BCs version of the Mesopotamians. Canaan is not the center of their empire, it is a vassal state. In first edition Irem had a war on its hands because the Canaan vassals fled further east and drew the attention of their masters. Ubar is never given a specific location but is heavily implied to be in somewhere in the land of two rivers as well, perhaps on the outlying northmost edge. Please do what we were told would be done back in the preliminary stages of the manuscript and correct your writing. At the very least it should be made crystal clear that the Ki-En-Gir are the ones in charge and Canaan is not the center of their empire. And as a general note I'd appreciate it if you paid a closer eye to the history you are telling, since a simple google search would have told you what the Ki-En-Gir really are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-17T18:08:02-08:00","id":1435802,"title":"","content":"Ki-En-Gir literally means &quot;country of the noble lords&quot; in Sumerian.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-17T19:05:41-08:00","id":1435806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435800-the-ki-en-gir-are-not-from-canaan#post1435800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, this was pointed out WAAAAAAY back in the first manuscript and we were given vague assurances it would be correct by this go round. Well, it hasn't been. Its very sloppy and it should be corrected as swiftly as possible.<br /> <br /> &quot;Canaan\u2019s own legions of professional soldiers, the Ki-En-Gir, had heeded the warnings of Irem\u2019s relentless campaign<br /> well in advance.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is a badly misunderstood reading of the first edition's history and a horribly researched bit of writing to boot. Ki-En-Gir, as noted many times by us and confirmed by the writers of first edition, refer to the 4000 Millenia BCs version of the Mesopotamians. Canaan is not the center of their empire, it is a vassal state. In first edition Irem had a war on its hands because the Canaan vassals fled further east and drew the attention of their masters. Ubar is never given a specific location but is heavily implied to be in somewhere in the land of two rivers as well, perhaps on the outlying northmost edge. Please do what we were told would be done back in the preliminary stages of the manuscript and correct your writing. At the very least it should be made crystal clear that the Ki-En-Gir are the ones in charge and Canaan is not the center of their empire. And as a general note I'd appreciate it if you paid a closer eye to the history you are telling, since a simple google search would have told you what the Ki-En-Gir really are.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>there is an errata submission link.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-17T22:43:42-08:00","id":1435818,"title":"","content":"You don't have to be so rude about it dude. You are capable of being polite"